<title>USA: US Home Builders-Market Index falls to 56 in April.</title>
<headline>US Home Builders-Market Index falls to 56 in April.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Association of Home Builders said its Housing Market Index fell two points to 56 in April from 58 in March.</p>
<p>Builders' ratings of single-family-home sales fell to 59 from 61 in March.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, traffic of prospective buyers declined four points to 45 in April from 49 in March. And the component index for single-family sales in the next six months dipped to 63 from 67 during the same period.  </p>
<p>A Housing Market Index over 50 generally means the number of positive responses received from builders exceeded the number of negative responses. The April index is based on the ratings of 383 respondents.</p>
